1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
Everyone wants to be happy.
We treat it as the whole point of being alive.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:09,500
But that chase rests on a belief —
that happiness is something you acquire.

3
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:14,500
Get it and you're bored.
Lose it and you ache. Pain is the constant.

4
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:16,800
Happiness is only the absence of pain.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,500
The relief when hunger ends isn't joy.
It's the pain of hunger leaving.

6
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:26,500
That comfort of stepping into warmth
out of the cold? Just cold, departing.

7
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:31,500
To be born is to begin hurting.
A body and a mind guarantee it.

8
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:35,500
Chasing more, in the name of happiness,
only deepens the emptiness.

9
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:39,500
Desire doesn't end when it's fed.
It grows a bigger mouth.

10
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:43,500
Whatever we own,
we are built never to be satisfied.

11
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:47,500
So you want to be happy?
Then be grateful for the moment going past right now.

12
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:53,500
A warm meal. Real sleep.
The voice of someone who loves you. That is enough.

13
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:56,500
If life hurts a little less,
it has already succeeded.

14
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:59,000
From "The Eyes That Read People",
by Baltasar Gracián.
